  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through Saturday)\nIssued at 1120 PM CDT Sat Oct 24 2026\n\nThe pattern aloft does flatten slightly by Tuesday allowing a \nweaker trailing wave to pass from SW TX into the Midwest by \nTuesday evening. Low level moisture will be lacking as the wave \npasses but a brief period of light showers may spread into E OK \nearly Tuesday. Any rainfall amounts will remain light. The pattern\nwill remain largely persistent through the work week with temperatures\nwell above seasonal normals. Winds may trend slightly stronger \nduring the afternoons which could locally raise fire weather \nconcerns.\n\nUncertainty does increase by late in the week into next weekend as\nthe pattern aloft will feature strengthening southwesterly flow\naloft and potential for one more more fast moving waves to pass\nacross the central CONUS. The potential for an associated cold\nfront to move into the region with the passing waves also adds\nuncertainty and guidance remains varied in both strength and\ntiming of any meaningful frontal passage. Rain chances will remain\nin the forecast for several days into next weekend until the\nevolving pattern can be better resolved.",
